'cos they were hungry.

00:12:21.040 --> 00:12:22.840
The thing is you're actually right,

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:27.240
because almost all the specimens now extant
were brought in by cats.

00:12:27.240 --> 00:12:28.350
Oh, as presents?

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:30.610
As presents for the lighthouse keeper,
you're absolutely right.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:34.490
Although, they're not presents.
They're sort of a mark of pity.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:37.650
Yes, it's that kind of,
"Look, that's how you do it", isn't it?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.270
It's the kind of thing they're showing you.

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.940
It's like when they s*** on the floor, it's
to show they're angry.

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:45.750
It's true. That's what happened when you came
to my house.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:49.270
What? You s*** on the floor
because you were angry he was there...?

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:50.270
"Out, Scott!"

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:52.640
Do you remember?
He once stayed over at my house.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:55.340
I did. God, that was before
your stag-do wasn't it?

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:58.020
Yeah. You stayed over at my house and I just
heard this immortal phrase,

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.060
"Gary? The cat's s*** on the floor."

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:02.640
I have no memory of this at all.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:06.140
That happened. It's the only time she's ever
done it with another person in the house.

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.290
Normally, we get it after a weekend away or
something,

00:13:08.290 --> 00:13:11.630
a day or so later she'll just go and lay one
on the floor to say,

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:14.040
"Damn it, you've been away and this is how
angry I am,

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.270
"I'm going to let you see this."

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:17.520
So for some reason,
she took with umbrage with you

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:21.270
to that degree that she did a massive dump
in protest.

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:23.780
And when I do it, it's wrong.

00:13:25.540 --> 00:13:28.940
On the other hand, I know exactly how my resignation
from the show is going to go,

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.730
should it ever happen.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:34.680
So, yes, what happened to most of the specimens?
Where did they end up?

00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:35.680
Museums!

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:38.460
Yes, absolutely right. What happened to most
of the cats?

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:39.860
Mew-seums.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:48.160
Shot, sadly. But there was a…

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:51.820
Oh, I like this one when it ends on dead cats.
It's always good fun isn't it?

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:53.800
And that's the end of the show!

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:56.670
It's not ending on that.
There was a recommendation sent out.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.350
What should lighthouse keepers not do?

00:13:58.350 --> 00:13:59.850
Have cats to shoot in the first place!

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:02.990
Yes. It was recommend that
they not introduce pests.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:06.720
So the last question, who was Lyall?

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:10.480
Who were they named after?
Lyall's wren, Traversia lyalli?

00:14:10.480 --> 00:14:12.440
Was he the lighthouse keeper?

00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:13.700
Yes, he was!

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:15.000
Hooray!

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:22.380
So at the end of the show, congratulations,
Chris, you win this one.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:28.200
You win a stuffed toy inspired by the villain
from 'Nightmare on Elm Street'.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.600
It's a Teddy Krueger.

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:32.610
With that, we say thank you to Chris Joel,

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:34.720
to Gary Brannan,

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:36.300
to Will Seaward.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.380
I've been Tom Scott
and we'll see you next time.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:42.720
Can I really go this time?

00:14:42.720 --> 00:14:43.320
Yes!

